# Hosts that execute keel's linux/amd64 vector code, one per line.
#
# Copy to .keel-hosts (gitignored) and edit. Requirements per host:
#   - amd64 with AVX2+FMA, and for the AVX-512 backend the F/CD/BW/DQ/VL
#     bundle that archsimd.X86.AVX512() gates on
#   - sshd with key auth from this machine; no Go toolchain needed
#   - for P2/P3 benchmark numbers, a fixed frequency governor
#
# Or set KEEL_REMOTE_HOSTS="host-a host-b", which takes precedence.
# See docs/hosts.md.
#
# Two more machine-local lists, same format, both read by scripts/gate-p3.sh:
#
#   .keel-openblas-hosts  ($KEEL_OPENBLAS_HOSTS) — hosts that can produce the
#     OpenBLAS reference for P3's >=60% criterion. Unlike the list above, these
#     DO need a Go toolchain, plus OpenBLAS, because the comparison is built
#     natively there so both halves of the ratio run in one invocation on one
#     machine. Empty means the criterion cannot be evaluated, which is a gate
#     failure, not a skip.
#
#   .keel-sentinel  ($KEEL_SENTINEL_HOST) — the host P2's throughput floor is
#     re-checked on, to notice a K-loop that P3 made fatter. Should be the host
#     that classifies issue-bound, since that is where instruction count binds.
#     Empty means every host is a sentinel: missing configuration costs time,
#     never coverage.

